NOTICE - third party AsyncAPI documents
=======================================

This directory holds AsyncAPI documents written by other people. They are vendored
here as test fixtures for the OPENREF event corpus, per SPEC 21 and BUILD T049.
Nothing here is part of any published OPENREF package: these files do not ship in a
tarball, are not linked into any consumer's code, and carry no obligation into it.

It is a second corpus root beside `packages/core/test/corpus` rather than more
documents inside it, for the reason the version history is a third: every file in the
HTTP corpus is normalized by `normalizeOpenApiDocument` and every file here by
`normalizeAsyncApiDocument`, so one directory would need a per file switch that says
which reader to use, and a document filed under the wrong reader would be refused
rather than mis-read only by luck.

This NOTICE exists because attribution has to travel with the material. `manifest.json`
next to it carries the same facts in machine readable form, and the license gate checks
that the two agree. A manifest line detaches the moment a file is copied out of this
directory on its own; a NOTICE in the directory does not.

Each document below is listed with its source, the date it was retrieved, its license,
its copyright holder, and whether OPENREF modified it. The documents are unmodified.
OPENREF claims no copyright in any of them, and their licenses are not changed by their
presence here. File names are OPENREF's, because two publishers use the same words for
different documents; the `source` line of each entry is the file as it stands upstream.

